{{Quote|The continued and inexplicable Ghorman resistance to Imperial norms. Terrorism strikes again in Ghorman. Just three weeks after events in Corei and Jel-Novi, there was a firebombing last night at the Naval Terminal in Palmo. You can see, behind me, vapor and thermal smoke still rising from the site&hellip;|A news reporter|audio=AfterEventsInCoreiAndJelNovi-Messenger.flac|<ref name="Messenger">{{Andor|Messenger (episode)}}</ref>}}
'''Jel-Novi''' was a location on the [[planet]] [[Ghorman]].<ref name="WAY" /> In [[2 BBY]], an [[event in Jel-Novi|event]] occurred in Jel-Novi which the [[Galactic Empire]] characterized as [[Terrorist|terrorism]]<ref name="Messenger" /> as part of their [[anti-Ghorman whispering campaign]], aiming to reinforce control of Ghorman so as to [[Mining|mine]] the planet's [[kalkite]]. The [[mineral]] was needed to coat the [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star's]] [[Hypermatter reactor|hypermatter annihilation reactor]]'s lenses as part of [[Darth Sidious|the Emperor's]] "[[Project Celestial Power|Energy Project]]."<ref name="OYL">{{Andor|One Year Later}}</ref>

Three [[Standard week|weeks]] after the event in Jel-Novi, following a [[Firebombing at the Imperial Naval Terminal|firebombing]] of the [[Imperial Naval Terminal]], an Imperial-aligned [[Unidentified reporter 1|reporter]] mentioned the event in Jel-Novi as an example of terrorism.<ref name="Messenger" /> [[Standard day|Days]] later, Imperial [[Starship|ships]] began unloading [[Mining rig|mining equipment]] in Jel-Novi to [[Gouge mining|mine]] Ghorman's kalkite deposits and provoke an [[Ghorman Massacre|uprising]] against the Empire to justify Imperial control of the planet. As protests broke out in Ghorman's [[capital]] [[city]] [[Palmo]] the next [[Local day|day]], [[Imperial Bureau of Standards]] employee [[Syril Karn]] mentioned the unloading of Imperial mining equipment in Jel-Novi to [[ISB Supervisor]] [[Dedra Meero]] when he confronted Meero on the true purpose of the Imperial presence on Ghorman.<ref name="WAY" />

==Behind the scenes==
Jel-Novi was first mentioned in "[[Messenger (episode)|Messenger]],"<ref name="Messenger" /> the seventh episode in the [[Andor Season 2|second season]] of the live-action [[Disney+]] series ''[[Star Wars: Andor]]'', which aired on [[May 6]], [[2025]].<ref name="Companion">{{InsiderCite|233|Andor Season 2 Companion|''Andor'' Season 2 Companion}}</ref>

